WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.410 --> 00:00:08.350
They’ve had enough: Enough of Thailand’s
military rulers, enough of seeing their rights

00:00:08.350 --> 00:00:15.110
curtailed, enough of promised elections being
pushed back time and time again.

00:00:15.110 --> 00:00:21.519
Now, these protesters in the heart of Bangkok
say, they won’t back down until the government

00:00:21.519 --> 00:00:25.140
makes good on its promise to let the people
have their say.

00:00:25.140 --> 00:00:31.980
We’ve been living with a parliament that
has no opposition for the last five years,

00:00:31.980 --> 00:00:38.280
without any good governance, no opposition
working in the parliament.

00:00:38.280 --> 00:00:44.840
So this election is very important for Thailand,
not only to go back to democracy but also

00:00:44.840 --> 00:00:49.370
to form the country back again.

00:00:49.370 --> 00:00:51.340
And to get their rights as citizens back.

00:00:51.340 --> 00:00:56.399
In the past five years, the military government
has used its power to stop critics from speaking

00:00:56.399 --> 00:00:58.530
out.

00:00:58.530 --> 00:01:02.809
Until recently, protests like this one were
prohibited by the strict assembly law Thailand’s

00:01:02.809 --> 00:01:04.790
military dictatorship put in place.

00:01:04.790 --> 00:01:10.110
Now that law has been lifted but inspite of
that protesters are still telling me they’re

00:01:10.110 --> 00:01:11.660
being harassed by the authorities.

00:01:11.660 --> 00:01:18.650
Last time, before I came to the demonstration,
the police called me and he tried to convince

00:01:18.650 --> 00:01:24.620
me and force me to not participate in the
demonstration and he tried to force me to

00:01:24.620 --> 00:01:34.390
go with him to the coffee shop and just put
me in the coffee shop until the demonstration

00:01:34.390 --> 00:01:37.360
ended.+o+
But these tactics aren’t keeping activists

00:01:37.360 --> 00:01:38.360
away.

00:01:38.360 --> 00:01:44.630
They’re afraid the government could play
for time until the election deadline set by

00:01:44.630 --> 00:01:45.670
Thailand’s constitution expires.

00:01:45.670 --> 00:01:50.680
Then, there would be no telling when Thais
would get to vote again.

